body:
You've duplicated the same code snippet, which differs only on one line (not counting indentation):

```c++
String err_text = vformat("Stack overflow. Check for infinite recursion in your script. Free stack: %d, used stack: %d, call depth: %d.", (uint64_t)frame - (uint64_t)top, (uint64_t)bottom - (uint64_t)frame, call_depth);

String err_text = vformat("Stack overflow. Check for infinite recursion in your script. Call depth: %d.", call_depth);
```

Instead, you could use a `has_overflow` flag and a string for the error details:

```c++
String err_details;

err_details = vformat("Free stack: %d, used stack: %d, call depth: %d.", (uint64_t)frame - (uint64_t)top, (uint64_t)bottom - (uint64_t)frame, call_depth);

err_details = vformat("Call depth: %d.", call_depth);

String err_text = "Stack overflow. Check for infinite recursion in your script. " + err_details;
```

